      "sourceTextSha256": "0c7faee64b7477bb085b46dbf8488208d2e8d8b6d3f069924b62e3b7b634ddc8",
      "text": "Day 2 · Breakfast, then a private panoramic city tour of La Candelaria, Bogotá’s historic centre (6 hours) with an English-speaking guide: the Gold Museum, with about 34,000 pieces of pre-Hispanic goldwork and more than 25,000 other pre-Columbian objects; the Casa de la Moneda and the Botero Donation; and a panoramic tour of Bolívar Square, with the Primatial Cathedral, the Casa de Nariño (the presidential palace), the Liévano Palace (City Hall) and the Palace of Justice. Finally, a coffee tasting: a local expert reveals the secrets of a good cup, its balance, body, aroma and acidity, and the most popular brewing methods, with a cup of specialty coffee and coffee-based treats. Note: the Gold Museum is closed on Mondays, and the Casa de la Moneda and Botero Donation on Tuesdays.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "word_exact",
        "fileId": "1Q09m42wkDEuSMhTW8fGBuIe2--u12XL1",
